IMPORT prelude

-- Prisons Act 1933 (Singapore) -- remission of sentences (Part 5B: ss 50E, 50G, 50H, 50I, 50J, 50K(3), 50N, 50S, 50T, 50ZA, 50ZB),
-- eligibility for home detention (ss 52, 53 and the Second Schedule), and the offence of conveying unauthorised articles into or out
-- of a prison (s 66).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PA1933.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 21 of 2025 (in force 17 August 2026) and S 561/2026 (in force 17 August 2026) shown. The arrangement of sections at the top of
-- the deposit is out of step with the body; the BODY's numbering is followed (unauthorised articles is s 66 in the body).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 19 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a prisoner, a prisoner's family
-- or a defence practitioner meets: when a remission order must be made and how long one runs, what breaks it and what the court may
-- add for breaking it, who may be released on home detention, and what a visitor must not bring in. Not encoded: prisons and
-- lock-ups, committees of inquiry, officers, custody and removal, the mandatory aftercare scheme and its First Schedule (Division 5),
-- life-sentence remission beyond s 50P's review (ss 50O-50R), the transitional Division 7 for offences before 1 July 2014, release
-- on licence (Part 5C), home-detention conditions, external placement and employment preparation (Parts 6A, 6B), prison offences
-- and punishments by the Superintendent, and Part 8.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Prisons Act 1933 -- release`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `50E, 50G, 50H, 50ZA, 50ZB -- who is entitled to remission`

-- s 50E(2): "Nothing in this Part applies to prisoners committed for debt."
-- s 50G: Division 2 applies to one or more terms "that is not a default sentence", and not where the prisoner "is also sentenced to
-- life imprisonment".
-- s 50H(1): a prisoner is "upon his or her admission to prison, entitled to have his or her sentence remitted"; (2) not where the
-- "aggregate term of imprisonment of 14 days or less"; (3) not where the sentence "consists wholly of" enhanced sentences under
-- s 50T(1)(a) or 50ZN, or terms for offences under s 50Y(1) (serious breach of a mandatory aftercare condition).
-- s 50ZA, 50ZB: a sentence consisting wholly of default sentences (imprisonment in default of paying a fine, s 2) is remitted on the
-- day a remission order would have been made under s 50I -- no order is needed.
GIVEN `committed for debt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sentenced to life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wholly default sentences` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wholly enhanced or aftercare-breach sentences` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `aggregate term in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prisoner is entitled to Division 2 remission` IF
        (NOT `committed for debt`)
    AND (NOT `sentenced to life imprisonment`)
    AND (NOT `wholly default sentences`)
    AND (NOT `wholly enhanced or aftercare-breach sentences`)
    AND `aggregate term in days` GREATER THAN 14

GIVEN `committed for debt` IS A BOOLEAN, `wholly default sentences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the default sentence is remitted without an order` IF
    (NOT `committed for debt`) AND `wholly default sentences`

§§ `50I -- when the remission order must be made`

-- s 50I(1)(a): the Commissioner "must make a remission order ... on the day after the day the prisoner has served whichever of the
-- following that ends later: (i) two-thirds of all the consecutive terms ...; (ii) 14 days of the prisoner's sentence".
-- (1)(b): where there are enhanced sentences (s 50T(1)(a), 50ZN) or s 50Y(1) terms AND other terms, the first limb becomes "the
-- aggregate of (A) all the [enhanced and s 50Y(1)] terms ... and (B) two-thirds of all the other consecutive terms". Enhanced time
-- earns no remission. With no enhanced terms (b) reduces to (a), so one formula serves both.
-- (2): NOT reckonable as served: "(a) one-third of any time ... confined in a punishment cell"; "(b) one-third of any time spent ...
-- in a hospital through his or her own fault or malingering"; "(c) any period of remission which is forfeited ..., unless ...
-- restored by the Superintendent"; "(d) any period of deferment ... ordered by the President"; (e) prescribed periods (not modelled).
-- Illustration (c): one year, 3 months in hospital through own fault -- order on 1 October 2013 (8 months plus 1 month).
-- Days are used throughout; the cases choose terms divisible by 3, since the Act says nothing about fractions of a day.
GIVEN `ordinary terms in days` IS A NUMBER, `enhanced or aftercare-breach terms in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reckonable days to be served` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`enhanced or aftercare-breach terms in days` PLUS `ordinary terms in days` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3) 14

GIVEN `punishment cell days` IS A NUMBER,
      `own-fault hospital days` IS A NUMBER,
      `forfeited remission days not restored` IS A NUMBER,
      `Presidential deferment days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days not reckonable` MEANS
        `punishment cell days` DIVIDED BY 3
    PLUS `own-fault hospital days` DIVIDED BY 3
    PLUS `forfeited remission days not restored`
    PLUS `Presidential deferment days`

-- The order is made on the day after this many days from the start of the sentence.
GIVEN `ordinary terms in days` IS A NUMBER,
      `enhanced or aftercare-breach terms in days` IS A NUMBER,
      `punishment cell days` IS A NUMBER,
      `own-fault hospital days` IS A NUMBER,
      `forfeited remission days not restored` IS A NUMBER,
      `Presidential deferment days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days before the remission order` MEANS
        `the reckonable days to be served` `ordinary terms in days` `enhanced or aftercare-breach terms in days`
    PLUS `the days not reckonable` `punishment cell days` `own-fault hospital days` `forfeited remission days not restored` `Presidential deferment days`

-- s 50I(3): the Commissioner "may defer making a remission order by not longer than 3 weeks in order to enable the execution of any
-- punishment ordered by the court" that has not been executed.
GIVEN `deferral in days` IS A NUMBER, `to execute an unexecuted court punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may defer the order` IF
    `to execute an unexecuted court punishment` AND `deferral in days` AT MOST 21

-- s 50I(4): where a prisoner "commits an offence while serving his or her sentence", the President may order the Commissioner not to
-- make a remission order, or to defer it, "if the President is of the opinion that the offence is a grave offence".
GIVEN `offence committed while serving` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President thinks it grave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may withhold remission` IF
    `offence committed while serving` AND `the President thinks it grave`

§§ `50J -- the 20-year review`

-- s 50J(1): where a prisoner "has served 20 years of his or her sentence but the Commissioner is not required to make a remission
-- order under section 50I, the Minister must review the prisoner's case" and may direct an order. (2) after a refusal, review "at
-- intervals not exceeding 12 months". Illustration: 24 years from 1 January 2013, s 50I order not due until 2035; review on
-- 1 January 2033 and, if refused, no later than 1 January 2034.
GIVEN `years served` IS A NUMBER, `a section 50I order is already required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must review the case` IF
    `years served` AT LEAST 20 AND (NOT `a section 50I order is already required`)

GIVEN `months since the Minister refused` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a further review is overdue` IF
    `months since the Minister refused` GREATER THAN 12

§§ `50K(3) -- what is suspended and what is remitted`

-- s 50K(3): with consecutive sentences, "apportion the total time ... served ... among each of the consecutive sentences (including
-- default sentences) as if each sentence is served in the same proportion"; the unserved portions of the non-default sentences are
-- added and SUSPENDED (remitted when the order expires, s 50K(1)(b)); (5) the unserved portion of a default sentence "is remitted upon
-- the making of the remission order". Illustration: 6 + 6 weeks plus a 3-week default sentence (105 days), order after 70 days --
-- 28 days suspended, 7 days of the default sentence remitted.
GIVEN `non-default days` IS A NUMBER, `default days` IS A NUMBER, `days served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unserved fraction` MEANS
    (`non-default days` PLUS `default days` MINUS `days served`) DIVIDED BY (`non-default days` PLUS `default days`)

GIVEN `non-default days` IS A NUMBER, `default days` IS A NUMBER, `days served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remainder suspended in days` MEANS
    `non-default days` TIMES `the unserved fraction` `non-default days` `default days` `days served`

GIVEN `non-default days` IS A NUMBER, `default days` IS A NUMBER, `days served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the default days remitted at once` MEANS
    `default days` TIMES `the unserved fraction` `non-default days` `default days` `days served`

§§ `50N -- extension while unlawfully at large`

-- s 50N(1): a person recalled under s 50X who "fails to report at such prison and on such date specified in the notice of recall" has
-- the remission order "extended by a period equivalent to the period the person remains unlawfully at large after the date so
-- specified". Illustration: expiry 31 December 2013, report due 15 December, reported 14 January 2014 (30 days late) -- new expiry
-- 30 January 2014. Days are numbered from 1 January 2013 = day 1.
GIVEN `expiry day` IS A NUMBER, `report due day` IS A NUMBER, `day actually reported` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the extended expiry day` MEANS
    IF `day actually reported` GREATER THAN `report due day`
    THEN `expiry day` PLUS (`day actually reported` MINUS `report due day`)
    ELSE `expiry day`

§§ `50S, 50T -- the basic condition and the enhanced sentence`

-- s 50S(1): the basic condition of every remission order is that the person "(a) must not commit any offence (not including an offence
-- under section 50Y(1)) while the remission order is in effect; and (b) must not be convicted of that offence and sentenced to" (i)
-- imprisonment "(not including a default sentence)", (ii) corrective training, (iii) reformative training, (iv) preventive detention,
-- (v) an SPP, (vi) an SEPP. A fine, or a default sentence, does not breach it.
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `a fine only`
    `a default sentence only`
    `imprisonment`
    `corrective training`
    `reformative training`
    `preventive detention`
    `an SPP`
    `an SEPP`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A Outcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the outcome is a qualifying sentence` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `a fine only` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a default sentence only` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `offence committed while the order is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence is under section 50Y(1)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the outcome` IS A Outcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basic condition is breached` IF
        `offence committed while the order is in effect`
    AND (NOT `the offence is under section 50Y(1)`)
    AND `the outcome is a qualifying sentence` `the outcome`

-- s 50T(1)(a): the court may add "imprisonment for a term not exceeding the remaining duration of the remission order, as determined
-- based on the date of the commission of the offence"; (b) any term or life if the order runs for natural life. (2)(b): the
-- aggregate of enhanced sentences for several offences must not exceed the remaining duration "based on the date of the earliest
-- offence". (4): "any extension of the duration of a remission order after the date of an offence ... is to be disregarded". (5):
-- enhanced terms "must run consecutively". Illustration: order to 31 December 2013, extended 7 days on 15 July, offence A on 1 August,
-- extended a further 10 days on 30 September, offence B on 21 October -- A capped at 1 August 2013 to 7 January 2014, B at 21 October
-- 2013 to 17 January 2014, both together at 1 August 2013 to 7 January 2014.
-- INFERENCE: "the length of the period from" one date "to" another is counted here inclusive of both days. The text does not say.
GIVEN `original expiry day` IS A NUMBER, `extension days before the offence` IS A NUMBER, `offence day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the enhanced sentence cap in days` MEANS
    `original expiry day` PLUS `extension days before the offence` MINUS `offence day` PLUS 1

GIVEN `total enhanced days` IS A NUMBER, `cap for the earliest offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enhanced sentences are within the aggregate cap` IF
    `total enhanced days` AT MOST `cap for the earliest offence`

§§ `52, 53 and Second Schedule -- home detention`

-- s 52: the Commissioner "may" release an eligible prisoner on home detention "for a period not exceeding 12 months" (or a period
-- the Minister prescribes in the Gazette -- not modelled).
-- s 53(1): eligible if (a) serving a term "of not less than 4 weeks"; (b) has served "not less than 14 days"; and (c) is not
-- disqualified under the Second Schedule. (2) the Minister may remove a disqualification. (3) consecutive terms are one sentence.
-- Second Schedule: disqualified if the prisoner (1) was previously released on home detention for the same sentence and that order
-- expired or was revoked; (2) is serving life; (3) had a death sentence commuted to life; (4) "is liable to be removed from
-- Singapore on completion of his or her sentence"; (5) is convicted under s 5, 7, 11F or 11H of the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973;
-- (6) is convicted of a listed Penal Code offence (among them s 147 rioting, s 354 outraging modesty, s 377BB voyeurism); (7) s 224
-- escape from custody; (8) Moneylenders Act 2008 s 19, 47 or 49; (9) Hostage-Taking Act 2010 s 3; (10) CYPA s 6 or 8 (on or after
-- 1 January 2020); (11) Tobacco and Vaporisers Control Act 1993 s 19B or 19C (S 525/2026, from 3 August 2026).
-- Penal Code s 379 theft and s 417 cheating (used in the Act's own illustrations) are not listed.
DECLARE Conviction IS ONE OF
    `Penal Code s 379 theft`
    `Penal Code s 417 cheating`
    `Penal Code s 147 rioting`
    `Penal Code s 354 outraging modesty`
    `Penal Code s 377BB voyeurism`
    `Penal Code s 224 escape from custody`
    `Misuse of Drugs Act s 5`
    `Misuse of Drugs Act s 8`
    `Moneylenders Act 2008 s 19`
    `Hostage-Taking Act 2010 s 3`
    `Tobacco and Vaporisers Control Act s 19B`

GIVEN `the conviction` IS A Conviction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction disqualifies` IF
    CONSIDER `the conviction`
    WHEN `Penal Code s 379 theft` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Penal Code s 417 cheating` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Misuse of Drugs Act s 8` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Prisoner
    HAS `term in days` IS A NUMBER
        `days served` IS A NUMBER
        `the conviction` IS A Conviction
        `previously on home detention for this sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
        `serving life` IS A BOOLEAN
        `death sentence commuted` IS A BOOLEAN
        `liable to removal from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Minister removed the disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A Prisoner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prisoner has a Second Schedule ground` IF
        `p`'s `previously on home detention for this sentence`
    OR  `p`'s `serving life`
    OR  `p`'s `death sentence commuted`
    OR  `p`'s `liable to removal from Singapore`
    OR  `the conviction disqualifies` (`p`'s `the conviction`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Prisoner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prisoner is disqualified` IF
    `the prisoner has a Second Schedule ground` `p` AND (NOT `p`'s `the Minister removed the disqualification`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Prisoner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prisoner is eligible for home detention` IF
        `p`'s `term in days` AT LEAST 28
    AND `p`'s `days served` AT LEAST 14
    AND (NOT `the prisoner is disqualified` `p`)

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home detention period is within s 52` IF
    `months` AT MOST 12

§§ `66 -- unauthorised articles, communications and recordings`

-- s 66(4): "unauthorised article" means "(a) any letter or document; (b) any electronic storage device; (c) any intoxicating
-- substance, controlled drug, psychoactive substance or stimulant; (ca) any Part 3A product; (d) any food or drink; (e) any item of
-- clothing; (f) money; or (g) any article not specifically authorised by the Commissioner to be brought into or out of a prison".
-- Items (a) to (f) are unauthorised outright; anything else is unauthorised unless specifically authorised.
-- s 66(1): any person who, "without the authority of this Act, the regulations made under this Act or the express permission of the
-- Commissioner", (a) conveys or supplies one to a prisoner, (b) brings or attempts to bring one into a prison, (c) brings one out or
-- conveys one from a prisoner, or (d) "makes any audio or visual recording in a prison" is guilty of an offence. (3): fine up to
-- $3,000, imprisonment up to 12 months, or both. (Limbs (e) and (f) -- incitement and prejudicing security -- are not modelled.)
DECLARE Article IS ONE OF
    `a letter`
    `a USB drive`
    `a packet of food`
    `a shirt`
    `cash`
    `a controlled drug`
    `a book`

GIVEN `the article` IS A Article, `specifically authorised by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the article is unauthorised` IF
    CONSIDER `the article`
    WHEN `a book` THEN NOT `specifically authorised by the Commissioner`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `giving it to a prisoner`
    `bringing it into a prison`
    `taking it out of a prison`

GIVEN `the article` IS A Article,
      `specifically authorised by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the conduct` IS A Conduct,
      `with express permission of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 66 is committed` IF
        `the article is unauthorised` `the article` `specifically authorised by the Commissioner`
    AND (NOT `with express permission of the Commissioner`)

GIVEN `made a recording in a prison` IS A BOOLEAN, `with express permission of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recording is an offence` IF
    `made a recording in a prison` AND (NOT `with express permission of the Commissioner`)

GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the punishment is within s 66(3)` IF
    `fine` AT MOST 3000 AND `months of imprisonment` AT MOST 12
